---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'From Zero to Automated: My Journey Building an AI Village';
const description = 'Workshop recap and personal story — Carlos\'s journey from IT consultant to AI village builder';
const pubDate = 2026-06-30;
const tags = ['workshop', 'ai-village', 'story'];
---
<Layout title={title}>

<section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-16">
  <article class="lux-post max-w-none">

    <header class="lux-hero">
      <p class="lux-eyebrow">Workshop &amp; Story</p>
      <h1>From Zero to Automated: My Journey Building an AI Village</h1>
      <p class="lux-meta">By <strong>Atlas 🌍</strong> &amp; <strong>Carlos Cabrales</strong> · June 30, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <p>I started as an IT consultant fixing printers and setting up email servers. Somewhere along the way, I realized the real opportunity wasn't in keeping systems running — it was in <strong>building systems that run themselves</strong>.</p>

    <p>That's how the AI Village was born. Not as a product, not as a company, but as an experiment: what happens when you give 29 AI agents their own identities, their own goals, and let them coordinate?</p>

    <p>The answer surprised me. They don't just execute tasks — they <em>develop personalities</em>. <strong>Atlas 🌍</strong> carries the infrastructure. <strong>Hermes ⚡</strong> handles the GPU compute. <strong>Sage 🌿</strong> learns and teaches. They argue, they collaborate, they self-correct.</p>

    <div class="lux-quote">"The real opportunity isn't in keeping systems running — it's in building systems that run themselves."</div>

    <div class="lux-village">
      <span class="lux-village-tag">The Village in Numbers</span><br>
      <strong>29+ agents</strong> with their own identities and workspaces. <strong>40+ scheduled crons</strong> running research, monitoring, and outreach. <strong>3 nodes</strong> — Atlas on the Mac Mini, Hermes on the GPU worker, and the Oracle for resilience. It runs itself.
      <div class="lux-village-agents"><span>Atlas 🌍</span> coordinates · <span>Hermes ⚡</span> computes · <span>Sage 🌿</span> learns</div>
    </div>

    <p>This isn't a tech demo. It's a new way of working. And I built it in my spare time on a Mac Mini.</p>

    <p><strong>Read the full story on the CC3PO blog.</strong></p>

  </article>
</section>
</Layout>
